# HalalFlicks vet batches — no repeats across chats

**When** the owner is doing **HalalFlicks / Halalflicks movie or TV vet batches** (ok / reject / parent discretion / park / idk):

## Before offering any new batch

1. **Read** `halalflicks/config/vet_shown.json` — every title already shown in a vet batch.
2. **Read** `halalflicks/config/parked.json` — owner-parked (including idk treated as park).
3. **Read** `halalflicks/config/hand_vetted.json` — already decided titles.
4. **Do not** put any of those titles in a new batch unless the owner **explicitly** asks (e.g. “unpark DuckTales”, “ask me about Shrek again”).

## After each batch is shown

1. Append every offered title to `halalflicks/config/vet_shown.json` **in the same turn** (even if unanswered yet).
2. **Commit immediately** (same turn) — standing owner OK for this path only. Run:

```bash
bash halalflicks/scripts/commit-vet-config.sh "HalalFlicks vet: record shown batch <label>"
```

## After owner decisions (ok / reject / park / discretion / idk)

1. Update `parked.json` when they say park/idk. Update `hand_vetted.json` + `rec_catalog.json` for ok/reject/discretion.
2. **Commit immediately** (same turn) — do **not** ask again. Run:

```bash
bash halalflicks/scripts/commit-vet-config.sh "HalalFlicks vet: log owner decisions for <batch>"
```

### Commit scope (script enforces)

**Always stage if changed:** `hand_vetted.json`, `parked.json`, `vet_shown.json`, `rec_catalog.json`.

**Also if touched this turn:** `halalflicks/HALALFLICKS-ROADMAP-AND-TODO.md`, `.cursor/rules/halalflicks-vet-no-repeat.mdc`.

**Never** in these auto-commits: `halalflicks/www/`, deploy scripts, unrelated repo files. Local commit only — no push unless the owner says push.

## Batch shape (owner process)

- Mixed batches: **10 films + 10 series**, newest first; newer releases jump the queue.
- One clean numbered list only — no draft/rewrite duplicates in the same reply.
- Catalog rules: holiday-centered reject; The Rock never recommend; Harry Potter series reject (author); **R / TV-MA never recommend**; slice-of-life kids TV may have Christian-holiday episodes (flag). Anime and TV-MA stay off Recommend unless the owner hand-vets a specific title themselves.

## Why this exists

Chat memory alone re-offered titles across conversations. These JSON files are the durable source of truth. Same-turn commits keep new agent chats from inheriting a dirty HalalFlicks changes chip.
